concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-torture-prohibition-and-death-penalty-abolition-act-2010-sch-1-sec-274-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "274 3  Prosecutions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-274-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Proceedings for an offence against this Division, where the conduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly outside Australia, must not take place except with the consent in writing of the Attorney-General.  (2) Even though a consent in accordance with subsection (1) has not been given in relation to an offence against this Division:  (a) a person may be arrested for the offence, and a warrant for the arrest of a person for the offence may be issued and executed; and  (b) a person may be charged with the offence; and  (c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail; but no further step in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) is to be taken until such a consent has been given.  (3) Subsection (2) does not prevent the discharge of the accused if proceedings are not continued within a reasonable time." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Proceedings for an offence against this Division, where the conduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly outside Australia, must not take place except with the consent in writing of the Attorney-General.  (2) Even though a consent in accordance with subsection (1) has not been given in relation to an offence against this Division:  (a) a person may be arrested for the offence, and a warrant for the arrest of a person for the offence may be issued and executed; and  (b) a person may be charged with the offence; and  (c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail; but no further step in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) is to be taken until such a consent has been given.  (3) Subsection (2) does not prevent the discharge of the accused if proceedings are not continued within a reasonable time."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c27a8d5a407d9f2b6a808389d26d04789c3b2224145cd18bca60d7586422d2d0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-torture-prohibition-and-death-penalty-abolition-act-2010-sch-1-sec-274-3-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-torture-prohibition-and-death-penalty-abolition-act-2010-sch-1-sec-274-3-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-torture-prohibition-and-death-penalty-abolition-act-2010-sch-1-sec-274-3-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-torture-prohibition-and-death-penalty-abolition-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-torture-prohibition-and-death-penalty-abolition-act-2010.pdf, p.9" .
